│     The bug was that `_encode_files` used `isinstance(fp, _SupportsRead)` to detect file-like objects. Since    │
│ `_SupportsRead` is a `runtime_checkable` protocol, it checks for the presence of the `read` method in the class │
│ hierarchy, but it does not detect methods provided via `__getattr__`. This caused `__getattr__`-based file      │
│ wrappers to be treated as raw data instead of files.                                                            │
│                                                                                                                 │
│     I replaced `isinstance(fp, _SupportsRead)` with `hasattr(fp, "read")` in `src/requests/models.py` within    │
│ the `_encode_files` method. This ensures that any object with a `read` method, including those using            │
│ `__getattr__` for proxying, is correctly identified as a file-like object and read accordingly.                 │
│                                                                                                                 │
│     Verified the fix with a reproduction script that uses a `__getattr__`-based wrapper around a `BytesIO`      │
